# @tcforce: rows with no @tcforce twin in freecam-corpus.manifest, with the
# retained terrain cache forced on (OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1; on the
# software rasteriser terrain otherwise draws through the CPU walk) and the
# first-touch bake budget off, as the @tcforce rows there. A row named after a
# row above is that row's twin. crystal-flight-skip-entry@tcforce has no plain
# twin: it boots into the level with no input and samples the start view, since
# the crystal_flight freecam rows look down from beyond the original-LOD draw
# distance and draw no terrain on the original-LOD leg.
gnasty_gnorc_attack@tcforce|1700|100||1796,1808|OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 OPENPETE_TC_BAKE_BUDGET_US=off
crystal-flight-skip-entry@tcforce|1700|2||1700|--skip-to-level crystal_flight OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 OPENPETE_TC_BAKE_BUDGET_US=off

# stone-hill-skip-fadein: the first gameplay renders after --skip-to-level.
# At VBL 1583 the title exit leaves D_80075950.post unwritten, so the first
# gameplay draw skips its VSync wait and the next tick renders in the same
# VBL: key 1584 is the present where both renders reach the native scene.
stone-hill-skip-fadein|1584|2||1584|--skip-to-level stone_hill
